+\paragraph{Does the fine-tune undo its start? (2026-10-29)}\label{par:ft_harm} The question of 2026-10-26: where a
+fine-tune loses to scratch at small $D$ (par.~\ref{par:nogain}, \ref{par:lowd_ft}, \ref{par:lowd_dyhpo}), does the
+pretrained model start better than scratch's best and the fine-tune lose it, or start worse and never get there?
+Asked before the model files of the finished runs are deleted, from what those runs saved. Per run, two readings
+of its validation (the MSE of $\log|\mathcal M|^2$): the start, the loss at step $0$, before any update, and the
+minimum of its validation curve, the run's value. A run that keeps the parent's head starts at the parent's output on
+the probe as it is; linear probe then fine-tune starts at the frozen trunk's ridge read-out, the head it is given;
+both come from the read-out jobs of par.~\ref{par:lowd_ft}, which built each cell's step-$0$ experiment. A run loses
+when its minimum is above scratch's best, and a losing run is (i) a start worse than scratch, improved on but never
+brought to scratch, (ii) a start already below scratch that the run loses, or (iii) a start worse than scratch that the
+run never even gets back to. The runs: the first round (four methods at the grid's best HPs on the $60$ cells), each
+method's best trial in the DyHPO round, and the grid's best default fine-tune. The grid has $101$ losing cells at
+$D\le10^{2.5}$ over the twelve probes and ten rungs, but its start is known only for the $13$ among the $60$ cells, where
+a read-out was run (\code{analysis/transfer/ft\_harm.py}, \code{data/ft\_harm.json}; the first round's curves copied
+from CC to \code{runs/zz\_lowd\_curves}, the DyHPO round's and the grid's already in \code{data/lowd\_dyhpo\_sweeps.json}
+and \code{scratch\_sweeps.json}; Fig.~\ref{fig:ft_harm}).
